    ['masala-chai-and-kulhad-culture-in-rajasthan', 'Masala Chai and Kulhad Culture in Rajasthan', 'Food', 'jawai-squirrel-chai',
     'Why a cup of tea in a clay cup is part of a village morning, and how to order it.',
     'Masala Chai and Kulhad Culture in Rajasthan: A Traveller’s Guide',
     'A guide to Rajasthani masala chai and kulhad tea: what goes in it, why clay cups, where to drink it and how to enjoy it on a safari morning.',
     'masala chai Rajasthan, kulhad chai, Rajasthani chai culture, village tea stall Rajasthan, chai on safari, Bera chai',
     'Tea is how Rajasthan starts the day. In villages around Jawai, a roadside stall is also where news is shared.',
     [['What makes it masala chai', 'Tea leaves boiled with milk, sugar and spices such as ginger and cardamom. Some stalls add black pepper or tulsi in winter. It is strong, sweet and hot.'],
      ['Why a clay cup', 'A kulhad is an unglazed clay cup that is used once and then returned to the soil. It adds an earthy flavour, and it is a more sustainable choice than plastic or paper.'],
      ['How to enjoy it', 'Drink it after a cold dawn drive, ask for less sugar if you prefer, and take your time. You will often find a stall near the village crossroads in Bera. Our café serves kulhad masala chai. See the [restaurant](restaurant).']],
     [['Is chai safe for sensitive stomachs?', 'It is boiled, so usually fine. Ask the team if you have concerns.'],
      ['Can I get tea without sugar?', 'Yes. Ask for “bina cheeni” or less sugar.'],
      ['Do you serve tea on early safaris?', 'We can help arrange a flask for the drive. Ask the team.']], 'food'],

    ['marwari-vs-mewari-food-differences-explained', 'Marwari vs Mewari Food: What Is Different on Your Plate', 'Food', 'food-thali-rajasthan',
     'Rajasthan’s cuisines vary by region. Here is how Marwar, where Bera lies, differs from Mewar around Udaipur.',
     'Marwari vs Mewari Food: Regional Differences in Rajasthan',
     'Marwari and Mewari food compared: dry-land dishes, grains, spices and sweets, and what to eat in Bera in the Marwar region versus Udaipur.',
     'Marwari food, Mewari food, Rajasthani regional cuisine, Marwar vs Mewar food, Pali Rajasthan food, Marwari thali',
     'Bera sits in Pali district, part of the Marwar region, while Udaipur is the heart of Mewar. The food shifts as you travel between them.',
     [['Marwar: food of the dry land', 'Marwari cooking suits a dry climate, so it leans on bajra, dried vegetables like ker and sangri, lentils, gram flour, ghee and yogurt. Dishes such as gatte ki sabzi, kadhi and dal baati churma are typical.'],
      ['Mewar: a little more variety', 'Mewar, around Udaipur, has more water and farmland. You see more fresh vegetables, maize and wheat, and some regional specialities in thali meals alongside the Rajasthani classics.'],
      ['What to eat in Bera', 'Village-style bajra roti with ghee, dal, kadhi, ker sangri and a sweet. Read our [dal baati churma guide](blog/dal-baati-churma-and-marwari-thali-guide) and [Rajasthani vegetarian food](blog/rajasthani-vegetarian-food-to-eat-in-jawai).']],
     [['Which cuisine does Jawai belong to?', 'Marwari, in the broader sense of the Pali and Jodhpur belt.'],
      ['Is Marwari food always spicy?', 'Not always. Heat comes from chutneys and pickles, and mild food is easy to request.'],
      ['Can I find both cuisines on a Jawai trip?', 'Yes. Udaipur adds Mewari variety on either side of your stay.']], 'food'],

