     [['Is Rajasthani breakfast vegetarian?', 'Almost always. Ask about Jain options if you need them.'],
      ['Is mirchi vada very spicy?', 'It can be. Ask for a mild chilli.'],
      ['Do you serve breakfast before the safari?', 'We can arrange a light early breakfast or a pack. Tell us the evening before.']], 'food'],

    ['village-walk-and-farm-visit-in-bera', 'A Village Walk and Farm Visit in Bera: What You Will See', 'Culture', 'jawai-village-hut',
     'A gentle, slow way to see daily life around Jawai, with etiquette tips for being a good guest.',
     'Village Walk and Farm Visit in Bera: What to Expect and Etiquette',
     'What a village walk in Bera is like: farms, wells, herding, temples and chai stops, plus respectful etiquette, best time and what to carry.',
     'Bera village walk, Jawai village tour, Bera farm visit, Rajasthan village experience, village visit near Jawai',
     'A walk through Bera is the best counterweight to the safari. It shows how people live in the landscape that leopards share.',
     [['What you will see', 'Mud and stone houses, wells, fields of wheat and mustard in winter, goats and cattle, shrines and school children. Farming and herding routines shape the day.'],
      ['How to do it well', '- Walk early in the morning or late afternoon. || - Go with a local guide or a team member. || - Greet people, smile and ask before taking photographs. || - Carry water and a hat, and wear closed shoes. || - Buy a snack or tea from a village stall.'],
      ['Being a good guest', 'Dress modestly, keep your voice low and never enter homes or fields without invitation. Do not give money or sweets to children. Read our [Bera village guide](blog/bera-rajasthan-village-guide).']],
     [['How long does a village walk take?', 'About one to two hours at an easy pace.'],
      ['Is it suitable for kids and seniors?', 'Yes, at a gentle pace on flat paths.'],
      ['Is a guide necessary?', 'Strongly recommended, for context, safety and respect.']], 'culture'],

    ['stargazing-in-jawai-dark-sky-guide', 'Stargazing in Jawai: A Dark-Sky Guide for Clear Rajasthan Nights', 'Experience', 'jawai-granite-plain',
     'With little light pollution, Jawai’s night sky is a quiet bonus. Here is how to make the most of it.',
     'Stargazing in Jawai: Dark-Sky Guide and Best Time',
     'How to enjoy stargazing in Jawai: best months, moon phases, where to look, what to bring, simple apps and photography tips.',
     'stargazing Jawai, Jawai night sky, star gazing Rajasthan, Milky Way Jawai, dark sky Bera, astrophotography Jawai',
     'Away from big cities, the sky around Bera is dark and often clear. A short evening outside can be the nicest end to a safari day.',
     [['When to look', 'Clear winter nights, roughly October to March, give the crispest skies. Nights around the new moon are the darkest. In the monsoon, clouds often block the view.'],
      ['What you can see', 'Bright planets, constellations and, on a dark, moonless night, the Milky Way. Your eyes need 15 to 20 minutes to adjust, so avoid looking at phone screens.'],
      ['Tips', '- Wear warm clothes because nights get cold. || - Use a star-map app in red or night mode. || - Bring a reclining chair or mat. || - For photos, use a tripod, a wide lens and a long exposure. || - A hot chai helps. We can often arrange a campfire evening at the hotel.']],
     [['Can I see the Milky Way in Jawai?', 'On clear, moonless nights away from lights, usually yes.'],
      ['Is it safe to stargaze near the hills?', 'Stay near the hotel or with a guide. Do not wander in leopard country at night.'],
      ['What is the best month?', 'December and January are cold but crystal clear, though October to March all work.']], 'stay'],

    ['rajasthani-handicrafts-to-buy-near-jawai', 'Rajasthani Handicrafts to Buy Near Jawai: Bandhani, Mojari and More', 'Culture', 'jawai-women-bangles',
     'A short shopping guide for souvenirs, with tips on where to buy them and how to spot quality.',
     'Rajasthani Handicrafts to Buy Near Jawai: Souvenir Guide',
     'What handicrafts to buy near Jawai: bandhani, leheriya, block prints, mojari shoes, silver jewellery, miniature paintings and puppets, and where to shop.',
     'Rajasthani handicrafts, bandhani, mojari shoes, block print Rajasthan, Udaipur shopping, Jodhpur shopping, souvenirs Rajasthan',
     'Bera itself has only simple shops, but Udaipur and Jodhpur are good places to pick up Rajasthani crafts before or after your stay.',
     [['Textiles', '- Bandhani: tie-dyed dupattas and sarees. || - Leheriya: wavy-striped turbans and fabrics. || - Block prints: hand-stamped cotton shirts, sheets and scarves.'],
      ['Other crafts', '- Mojari: embroidered leather shoes. || - Silver jewellery and lac bangles. || - Miniature paintings, especially in Udaipur. || - Wooden toys and puppets.'],
      ['Buying wisely', 'Ask where and how an item is made, bargain politely in markets and look for fixed-price government emporiums if you want certainty. Choose items made by local artisans. Buy a cup of chai in Bera and support village families directly.']],
     [['Where can I shop for crafts near Jawai?', 'Udaipur and Jodhpur have the best choice. Bera has basic shops only.'],
      ['Is bargaining expected?', 'In markets, yes, politely. Fixed-price shops exist too.'],
      ['What is a good light souvenir?', 'A block-print scarf or a small bandhani piece packs easily.']], 'culture'],
